  "description": "Calculus for the Epsilon symbolic math library. Gradients, directional derivatives, divergence, curl and potentials, Hessians, Laplacians and the second-derivative test for functions of several variables, as vectors and matrices of expressions that compile to fast delegates. Taylor, Laurent and Puiseux series with exact coefficients, and exact limits at a point, from either side and at infinity, by Gruntz's algorithm. Exact antiderivatives from a table of integrals, by substitution, by parts, by partial fractions with Hermite's reduction (over the roots of cubic and quartic factors in radicals too), by Bioche's rules and t = tan(x/2) for rational functions of sin and cos, by t = exp(x) and by trigonometric, hyperbolic and Euler substitutions for square roots of quadratics. Exact definite integrals, improper ones included, from the antiderivative with its singular points and jumps checked, and from a table of classic integrals such as the Gaussian, Dirichlet and Fresnel integrals. Line integrals by arc length and along vector fields. Numeric definite integrals by the tanh-sinh and exp-sinh rules over finite and infinite intervals, oscillating ones included, split at the singularities, kinks and peaks found in the expression, accurate at singular ends, and with divergent integrals reported instead of returned as numbers.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
